173
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:19,425
[SPEAKER_03]: What is something that, instead of like, let me do this, let me rehearse this idea, or think about it like this, what is something that you need to not do?

174
00:21:33,165 --> 00:21:34,426
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly, yeah.

175
00:21:35,106 --> 00:21:44,233
[SPEAKER_03]: So, if you have the pressure, if you recognize that you have this pressure to, okay, I need to find this or any other sort of pressure, you need to

176
00:21:46,078 --> 00:21:51,522
[SPEAKER_01]: Tame that first, and then you can... you will be able to, like, not even find it.

177
00:21:51,562 --> 00:21:53,104
[SPEAKER_01]: You will see, oh, it was already there.

178
00:21:53,184 --> 00:21:55,245
[SPEAKER_01]: I was just overlooking it because of this pressure.

179
00:21:56,066 --> 00:21:57,487
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's the key.

180
00:21:58,408 --> 00:22:07,515
[SPEAKER_01]: Rather than trying to to find the body so that the pressure will go away, practically speaking, more often than not, it will be the other way around.

181
00:22:07,956 --> 00:22:09,357
[SPEAKER_01]: Especially if you don't have the right idea yet.

182
00:22:09,417 --> 00:22:12,559
[SPEAKER_01]: It will be undo the pressure first,

183
00:22:13,466 --> 00:22:20,008
[SPEAKER_01]: By restraining, you're acting out of it, and that will then eventually reveal the body.

184
00:22:20,048 --> 00:22:26,310
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you... just a basic question, like, why am I doing this?

185
00:22:26,851 --> 00:22:29,672
[SPEAKER_01]: Why do I want to find the physicality?

186
00:22:30,992 --> 00:22:53,080
[SPEAKER_03]: And if you arrive at the answer that there's just this ambiguous restlessness, pressure, craving there, then you need to kind of rein in your mind, hold it back from that, and then, once that comes down, you would be able to recognize what's already there.

187
00:22:53,100 --> 00:22:56,341
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, again, it's like that simile that the Buddha gave

188
00:22:57,462 --> 00:23:07,146
[SPEAKER_01]: When the pond has been stirred up and all the mud in the pond is moving around, you can't see what's underneath.

189
00:23:08,026 --> 00:23:15,989
[SPEAKER_01]: And so, the way to still it is not to concentrate on some object that's ironically going to

190
00:23:16,689 --> 00:23:25,193
[SPEAKER_01]: The secondary to the physicality is to stop giving in to these unwholesome activities that may seem totally justified.

191
00:23:25,553 --> 00:23:28,235
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, see, I'm trying to practice and all that stuff.

192
00:23:28,855 --> 00:23:32,257
[SPEAKER_01]: But, again, wholesome and unwholesome is determined by the intention behind it.

193
00:23:32,337 --> 00:23:37,860
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if it's an intention of restlessness and craving, then that will obstruct

194
00:23:38,660 --> 00:23:41,622
[SPEAKER_01]: You're clear-seeing, whether you like it or not.

195
00:23:44,263 --> 00:24:05,455
[SPEAKER_01]: But again, if you haven't abandoned the even coarser unwholesome activities, where you're still, on account of these pressuring thoughts, acting out by body and speech, towards sensuality and aversion, then there's no hope that you can undo

196
00:24:06,036 --> 00:24:07,542
[SPEAKER_01]: The pressure is on this mental level.

197
00:24:07,662 --> 00:24:10,494
[SPEAKER_01]: But if all that other stuff has been taken care of beforehand,

198
00:24:11,237 --> 00:24:19,642
[SPEAKER_01]: Then you're just left with this, and then it's a matter of applying the same principle that you did, really, with your virtue.

199
00:24:19,702 --> 00:24:26,987
[SPEAKER_01]: You didn't try to, like, prevent the options to break the precepts from existing.

200
00:24:27,347 --> 00:24:36,712
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't, like, go out into the world and destroy all the alcohol there is in order to keep the precept of not drinking and all... and so on.

201
00:24:37,393 --> 00:24:40,535
[SPEAKER_01]: You just, while the option to do it is there, you don't give in to it.

202
00:24:41,255 --> 00:24:43,957
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's the same when you have these mental pressures.

203
00:24:44,798 --> 00:24:50,723
[SPEAKER_01]: You will have the craving to do something, whatever it might be.

204
00:24:51,183 --> 00:24:56,047
[SPEAKER_01]: And in this case, to find the physicality that's coming through that sense of restlessness.

205
00:24:56,308 --> 00:25:02,773
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, well, you don't try to just remove it, because that's going to be another restlessness.

206
00:25:03,734 --> 00:25:08,458
[SPEAKER_01]: Instead, you just see, okay, well, I'll endure this infinitely, because

207
00:25:09,657 --> 00:25:11,498
[SPEAKER_01]: In and of itself, it has arisen on its own.

208
00:25:11,538 --> 00:25:23,844
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if I imply that I need to get rid of it, that's going to be taking ownership of it, and that's, again, going to obscure whatever you may need to see.

209
00:25:23,904 --> 00:25:37,371
[SPEAKER_03]: So, in a way, you could say, when you have... when you no longer care as much about finding the physicality, that's when you'll be able to do it.

210
00:25:41,180 --> 00:25:43,182
[SPEAKER_01]: But you certainly need to keep trying to discern.

211
00:25:43,242 --> 00:25:48,307
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not like you just throw your hands up in the air and wait for it to arise.

212
00:25:48,827 --> 00:25:50,208
[SPEAKER_01]: There has to be the effort.

213
00:25:50,449 --> 00:25:54,532
[SPEAKER_01]: But you realize 99% of the effort is indirect.

214
00:25:54,833 --> 00:26:02,660
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the effort of undoing what obstructs the recognition and not just to kind of fabricate the recognition.

215
00:26:06,648 --> 00:26:25,188
[SPEAKER_02]: So, would that be correct to say, it's good to practice including these thoughts of... pressuring thoughts of finding the physicality into the pressure?

216
00:26:26,088 --> 00:26:26,789
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

217
00:26:27,470 --> 00:26:36,304
[SPEAKER_03]: And because, see, any thought, that's actually the crucial thing, because, like, again, if you've been keeping virtue,

218
00:26:37,546 --> 00:26:55,321
[SPEAKER_01]: If you have thoughts about covetousness, and greed, and fantasizing about things you want, and hating, and being annoyed at certain people, or whatever, you will recognize those thoughts quite easily, and you will be able to restrain them.

219
00:26:56,102 --> 00:27:05,190
[SPEAKER_01]: But, eh... when it comes to these other things, that are slightly more subtle, and might even feel justified, like I said before, eh...

220
00:27:06,712 --> 00:27:13,495
[SPEAKER_01]: It's... most of the time you'll get dragged by it, because it just feels just so personal.

221
00:27:14,076 --> 00:27:17,698
[SPEAKER_01]: It's kind of like you just almost automatically take it for granted.

222
00:27:18,438 --> 00:27:25,902
[SPEAKER_03]: So, yeah, very much it has to be included, because at the end of the day, a pressure is a pressure.

223
00:27:27,182 --> 00:27:32,645
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't want to be justifying or kind of

224
00:27:34,317 --> 00:27:51,709
[SPEAKER_01]: Acting as if some pressures are fine, if you want to overcome the hindrances, which are what obstructs the recognition of the physicality, then you need to be careful with any direction that involves pressure, because that's what the hindrances are.

225
00:27:51,929 --> 00:27:52,949
[SPEAKER_01]: It's any type of pressure.

226
00:27:54,364 --> 00:28:08,327
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it's often this tendency for people to justify, like, no, no, I know that I'm acting out of hindrances, but I just hope that this is kind of like the right acting out.

227
00:28:08,527 --> 00:28:16,009
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if I just keep going there, eventually, like, somehow, I'll arrive at this thing that I'm looking for.

228
00:28:16,729 --> 00:28:21,110
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not a very realistic hope.

229
00:28:22,411 --> 00:28:28,258
[SPEAKER_01]: And you basically just wind yourself up and take yourself farther away from it.

230
00:28:28,579 --> 00:28:33,685
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you'll just be kind of... at some point, you'll give up on it.

231
00:28:34,186 --> 00:28:37,510
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, maybe, you'll have the chance to find it.

232
00:28:37,610 --> 00:28:39,853
[SPEAKER_01]: But, see, you can prevent that entire thing.

233
00:28:40,814 --> 00:28:47,123
[SPEAKER_03]: You can prevent that entire wasted effort by just, from the very beginning, realize, okay, this is a pressure I shouldn't be acting out of.

234
00:28:47,143 --> 00:28:54,833
[SPEAKER_03]: So... and, yeah, like... because, again, it's not only about the physicality.

235
00:28:56,255 --> 00:28:57,657
[SPEAKER_01]: If you see pressure as pressure,

236
00:28:58,648 --> 00:29:00,608
[SPEAKER_01]: You're also developing yonisonma-sikāra.

237
00:29:01,529 --> 00:29:03,189
[SPEAKER_01]: So, eh...

238
00:29:03,909 --> 00:29:04,129
[SPEAKER_00]: It's...

239
00:29:04,149 --> 00:29:07,590
[SPEAKER_00]: The reader was recognizing all the five holding advocates, basically.

240
00:29:07,690 --> 00:29:07,870
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

241
00:29:07,930 --> 00:29:14,171
[SPEAKER_03]: So, if, if, if right now you're being pressured to recognize the body, well, contemplate what feeling is there.

242
00:29:14,371 --> 00:29:14,591
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

243
00:29:16,471 --> 00:29:19,652
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it an unpleasant feeling that's there on account of me not seeing the body?

244
00:29:20,492 --> 00:29:24,853
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you take it through that angle, that's already mindfulness.

245
00:29:25,213 --> 00:29:26,933
[SPEAKER_01]: It may not be the mindfulness you wanted,

246
00:29:28,493 --> 00:29:29,633
[SPEAKER_01]: But, that doesn't matter.

247
00:29:30,073 --> 00:29:30,974
[SPEAKER_01]: The point is to...

248
00:29:31,174 --> 00:29:32,534
[SPEAKER_01]: Most of the time, that's the better mindset.

249
00:29:32,554 --> 00:29:33,014
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

250
00:29:33,494 --> 00:29:36,035
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it's the one you need, not the one you want.

251
00:29:36,055 --> 00:29:37,715
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

252
00:29:38,996 --> 00:29:40,976
[SPEAKER_03]: So, again, being mindful of your intention.

253
00:29:41,016 --> 00:29:42,076
[SPEAKER_01]: Why am I trying to do this?

254
00:29:43,137 --> 00:29:48,118
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh... that is the proper mindfulness, the proper yonisonisakāra, then and there.

255
00:29:49,318 --> 00:29:54,041
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you stick to it, then maybe, you will get to see the body on the same peripheral level.

256
00:29:54,181 --> 00:30:01,185
[SPEAKER_01]: But, you have to be careful that the attempt is again not rooted in the same pressure, like we said before.

